# The FromCSharp sample copy each --integration-lt shard edits (LiveTestingShards.sampleCopy).
SageFs.Tests/fixtures/LiveTestingSample/.runs/

# Agent scratch. NEVER a product artifact.
#
# 21 files from .roastscratch were committed by accident at 53ae96d0, and 6
# from a $COMMANDCODE_SCRATCHPAD directory at c86c3402. Scratch is evidence
# FOR a decision, not a deliverable: it is unversioned, unreviewed, and has no
# owner, so checking it in only widens the surface someone has to keep correct.
# If a script is worth keeping it belongs in `scripts/` and earns a test; if a
# finding is worth keeping it belongs in a document.
#
# The harness path is literally `$COMMANDCODE_SCRATCHPAD` — a SHELL VARIABLE,
# not a placeholder. A pattern reading `commandcode_scratchpad` does not match
# it, and six files got committed because the rule looked correct and was not.
.roastscratch/
commandcode_scratchpad/
**/commandcode_scratchpad/
**/\$COMMANDCODE_SCRATCHPAD/

# GENERATED at build time into $(TargetDir) by the GenerateHostManifest target
# in SageFs.Host.fsproj — which is `bin/`, not here. The copy at the project ROOT
# is a build artifact that leaked into tracking, and it records whatever version
# happened to be current when it was written, so a tracked copy ships a stale
# version claim. The real manifest is the one in the build output, and the host
# reads that one. Untracked in ce63f746; this rule stops it coming back.
SageFs.Host/host-manifest.json

# The compiled Claude Code hook, written here by `dotnet fsi tools/agent-hooks/publish.fsx`
# (about 90 MB: self-contained, single file). Built per machine, never committed.
tools/agent-hooks/sagefs-repl-guard
tools/agent-hooks/sagefs-repl-guard.exe
